# Secrets the register / submit-run functions need beyond what Supabase
# injects automatically (SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY).
#
# Local dev: copy this to supabase/functions/.env (gitignored) and fill in
# real generated values — see the "Local development" section of
# supabase/README.md for a one-liner to generate them.
#
# Production: set with `supabase secrets set --env-file <file>`, or one at a
# time with `supabase secrets set NAME=value`. Never commit real values.
# Rotate all three if either the repo or a deploy log is ever exposed.

# HMAC key (base64) — hashes normalised emails/phones for dedupe. Never used
# to encrypt anything reversible; a leak of this key only lets someone test
# "does this email exist", not read one.
EMAIL_HASH_SECRET=

# AES-256-GCM key (base64, 32 raw bytes) — encrypts the actual email/phone
# columns. This is the one key that matters most: holding it is equivalent to
# holding every entrant's contact details in plain text.
EMAIL_ENC_KEY=

# HMAC key (base64) — signs play-token capability strings. Compromising this
# lets someone forge a token id's signature, but RLS still means they'd need
# a real token id from somewhere; it is defence in depth, not the only lock.
TOKEN_SECRET=
